    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: when more than 80 owners have already been created today, the owner response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\nI followed the same \"derive-at-creation, persist, read back\" pattern the codebase already uses for `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, and `householdId`:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 after the existing quota/derivation steps, sets the flag via a new `exceedsBulkSignupThreshold(owner)`. It reuses the exact accumulation path as the daily-limit rule (`countOwnersRegisteredOn(day)`, keyed on the owner's `registrationDate` which the controller defaults to today), and returns `true` when that count is `> 80`. Since the count is taken before persisting, it reflects owners already created that day.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a mapping expression that coerces a `null` stored value to `false`, guaranteeing the field is always present (satisfying \"otherwise false\" even for pre-existing/seed owners).\n\n5. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` passes: a fresh create returns `$.bulkSignupWarning == false`.\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThe `>80` branch shares the daily-limit counting path, so it accumulates identically once more than 80 owners exist for the day.",
